<title>NORWAY: Kvaerner sells Amec shares.</title>
<headline>Kvaerner sells Amec shares.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Anglo-Norwegian construction and engineering group Kvaerner ASA said on Thursday it had sold its stake in Britain's Amec Plc for 850 million crowns ($121.2 million) and would book a profit from the deal of 230 million crowns.</p>
<p>Kvaerner held 52,788,115 shares in Amec following a failed takeover attempt in 1995. ($ = 7.010 Norwegian Crowns)</p>
